    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102887" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεκνοῦς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦσσα</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦν</span>, 
			contr.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεκνόεις, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εσσα</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εν</span></span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>having children</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνανδρος ἢ τεκνοῦσσα</span> (Brunck for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεκνοῦσα</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεκοῦσα</span>) <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				308
			</span></i> (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παιδοῦς</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; οἶνον, ὃς . . τὰς γυναῖκας
					τεκνούσσας ποιεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>HP</u>
					9.18.10
				</span></i>
			, as cited by <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				1.31f
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεκνούσας</span> codd.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτέκνους</span> codd.<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ τεκνοῦσαι</span>, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ ἀειπάρθενοι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				56.10
			</span></i> codd.</div>
